        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "9114faf14d7047c4bdf761421378a089b356e960",
            "parents": [
                "48f2c87527c2ecaa98562fce65539ce596339cd7"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/15/87415/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                "username": "dkodihal"
            },
            "createdOn": 1770880614,
            "author": {
                "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                "username": "dkodihal"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "docs/platform_configuration.md",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall the feature sounds like an interesting use-case to me, maybe it would help to make a configuration example for the commit message to see how it would be used on your system."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/platform_configuration.md",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, child commits will show concrete/tested on upstream examples. Those already existed (MCTP over USB on Nvidia upstream platform) - I'm addressing Ed's comments on adding MCTP over USB as a platform schema/config as opposed to a regular/entity config."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/platform_configuration.md",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Does `configurations/<vendor>/` work as well?\n\nThen it would land in the existing destination directory on the BMC rofs and require less extra work. Otherwise you would have to decide on where to install it and add the extra directories into the EM implementation.\n\nSince there's a `Type` on these configs i don't think they will be hard to find and the `configurations` directory is already organized by vendor and platform."
                },
                {
                    "file": "docs/platform_configuration.md",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I moved platform/ under schemas/ (and under configurations/). This wat the existing scripts work."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 141,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "For the probe, please either break that out in the toplevel EM config and `$ref` to it here or re-write it as either array or single string.\n\n\nWriting it as array of string is not much more overhead than writing it as a single string and having less alternatives to write it simplifies things for the user."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 141,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "As written EM would create an interface `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Platform`\n\nwhich is not documented, i cannot find it currently. Do you want to document such an interface or alternatively prevent EM from creating it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't have a strong opinion about either of the above or leaving it as is (current behavior). Will hear from @ed@tanous.net as well. Keeping this comment unsresolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Resolving this - atm I have made no change. Will let maintainer(s) comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 163,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Please remove it here.\n\nWe don't need 2 ways to configure this and we don't need the indentation bloat introduced by the array.\n\nIt's just confusing for users to have 2 ways of doing things."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/global.json",
                    "line": 163,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/platform_schemas/platform_exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "`schemas/platform_schemas` is a bit redundant; maybe just `schemas/platform`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/platform_schemas/platform_exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/platform_schemas/platform_exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "If it's a configuration then it probably needs a schema with the properties listed.\n\nThere's only `Name` and `Type` currently.\n\nI don't think we can introduce any free-form configuration record.\n\nWhich properties can be configured needs to be known from the schema at build time since that's when configurations are validated."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/platform_schemas/platform_exposes_record.json",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "That's happening in the child commit. As I mentioned in that commit, I can squash commits if need be. At the moment I wanted to keep this separate to get feedback on the concept."
                }
            ],
